-- title:
--   Reduction at infinity intertwines T_ℓ with differential Hecke operator
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $p$, an integer $M \ge 1$ with $p \mid M$ and $p^2 \nmid M$, and a subgroup $H \le (\mathbb{Z}/M)^\times$ containing every unit $u$ whose image under `ZMod.unitsMap` along $M/p \mid M$ is $1$. Let $K$ be an algebraically closed field that is an algebra over $\mathbb{Z}/p$, let $S$ be a set of naturals, and write $\Gamma' =$ [`CohCarrier.GammaH`](def/CohCarrier_Level.html#L133) $(M/p)$ of `infSubgroup` $p\,M\,H$, the image of $H$ in $(\mathbb{Z}/(M/p))^\times$; here `GammaH` is the image in $SL_2(\mathbb{Z})$ of the preimage of the subgroup under the lower-right-entry character on $\Gamma_0$. Let $\rho$ be a $K$-linear map from $K \otimes_{\mathbb{Z}/p}$ `IntTwoCuspForms` $M\,H\,p$ — the quotient of the two-cusp integral lattice of weight-two cusp forms on `GammaH` $M\,H$ (those $f$ all of whose `heckeRingH` translates have $q$-coefficients in the bottom subring of $\mathbb{C}$, before and after the weight-two Atkin–Lehner slash at $p$) by `intIdeal` $p$ — to the Kähler differentials $\Omega[$`qExpFunctionFieldC` $K\,\Gamma'/K]$, the $K$-subfield of $K((q))$ generated by integral form ratios. Assume $\rho$ satisfies `IsInfReductionMap`: for every such integral $f$ and every integral power series $p_f$ realising the $q$-expansion of $f$, the series `diffQExp` of $\rho(1 \otimes \bar f)$ is the image of $p_f$ in $K((q))$. Let $\ell$ be a prime with $\ell \notin S$ and $\ell \nmid M$. Then $\rho$ composed after the base change to $K$ of the reduced generator `intTwoCuspGenMod` at `Gen.T` $\ell$ equals `genDiffModL` at `Gen.T` $\ell$ — namely `heckeDiffModLH` $K\,(M/p)$ `infSubgroup` $\ell$ — composed after $\rho$.
--
--   This is the Hecke-equivariance of the reduction map onto the component through the cusp $\infty$ of the special fibre at $p$: the operator $T_\ell$ for $\ell \nmid M$ on weight-two two-cusp integral forms mod $p$ of level $\Gamma_H(M)$ corresponds to the Hecke correspondence $T_\ell$ acting on differentials of the level-$(M/p)$ curve in characteristic $p$. It feeds the identification of the mod-$p$ two-cusp forms with the dual of the multiplicative part of the Tate module in the ordinary case, and the Atkin–Lehner twisting comparison for $T_\ell$.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_IsInfReductionMap_comp_baseChange_genT_eq_genDiffModL_comp.lean

